.TH FPRINTF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fprintf \- write formatted output to a Crunch stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fprintf(struct FILE* " stream ", const char* " format ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes formatted bytes without adding a newline. The supported conversions are
.BR %d ,
.BR %ld ,
.BR %lld ,
.BR %u ,
.BR %lu ,
.BR %zu ,
.BR %llu ,
.BR %x ,
.BR %lx ,
.BR %llx ,
.BR %f ,
.BR %.17g ,
.BR %Lf ,
.BR %.17Lg ,
.BR %s ,
.BR %c ,
and
.BR %% .
The compiler accepts up to 127 additional numeric or byte-pointer arguments
for this library function.
Extra arguments are evaluated but not used.
Corresponding signed and unsigned integer argument types are accepted when
the value is representable in both types.
Conversions other than
.B %%
accept a literal decimal width up to 2147483647 and the
.B \-
and
.B 0
flags. Fields are right-aligned with spaces by default;
.B \-
left-aligns, while
.B 0
zero-pads numeric values after any minus sign.
.B \-
overrides
.BR 0 ,
which is ignored for strings and characters.
.B %.17g
rounds binary64 values to 17 significant digits, ties to even, independent of
the floating-point environment.
.B %Lf
and
.B %.17Lg
format the full binary80 range, rounding ties to even independently of the
floating-point environment. Non-finite values are printed as
.B inf
or
.BR nan ,
without zero padding.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes written, or \-1 for an invalid format, missing or
incompatible argument, null format or string, unsupported real value,
unrepresentable count, or output error. A prefix may already have been written.
An output error sets
.B errno
and the stream error indicator. A null stream fails with
.BR EINVAL ,
even for an empty format. No particular errno or stream indicator is guaranteed
for format errors.
.SH NOTES
I/O is unbuffered. Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects. Other precisions, dynamic widths and other flags are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fwrite (3crunch),
.BR fputs (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch)
